      "writtenOn": "2023-10-04T16:29:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The STM32 options bytes are basically a separate region of flash memory that provide a way to pre-configure the chip before powering up. They are automatically loaded after POR and can enable/disable/configure features like RDP (readout protection), WRP (write protection), watchdogs, boot configurations, etc. Does the npcx have anything like this?",
      "parentUuid": "6b28b69a_811eb6ee",
      "revId": "661967462a946c1854cc29eeb90fd9ea81235231",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
